 "camera_idea": {
  "name": "The counter that changes hands",
  "why": "The sweet-shop counter is the seat of power, so every era of the story is told by WHO stands behind it: the uncle alone, Rafi behind it while the nephew learns in front, Rafi driven to the neighbour's counter for half pay, and finally Rafi back behind a counter he partly owns. The camera crosses from the customer side to the owner side whenever the power moves.",
  "signature": "The home door: the uncle arrives through the same dark doorway three times - firing, scheming, begging - and the third arrival is a night knock staged from further away, so his fall reads in the framing."
 },
